3301:		    this file uses the mode-aware one, and that difference is
3302:		    deliberate rather than an oversight -- recorded here
3303:		    because it has been re-filed as a defect more than once.
3304:		    FSRRA is an APPROXIMATION instruction, so there is no
3305:		    rounding mode for it to honour and `1.0f / sqrt()` is
3306:		    already a different approximation from the silicon's
3307:		    table-driven one.
3308:
3309:		    *** THIS COMMENT USED TO CITE "the SH-4 manual" FOR AN
3310:		    ERROR BOUND, AND THAT CITATION CANNOT BE CHECKED HERE --
3311:		    corrected 2026-08-22 when real manuals were obtained.
3312:		    FSRRA APPEARS IN NEITHER OF THEM. *** Zero hits in the
3313:		    SH-4 Software Manual (Rev. 5.0) and zero in the SH7750
3314:		    Hardware Manual (Rev. 7.00); the error-bound text those
3315:		    greps do find belongs to FIPR, a different instruction.
3316:		    FSRRA is an SH-4A addition, and the SH-4 opcode table has
3317:		    no entry for 1111nnnn01111101 at all, though its
3318:		    neighbours FSTS/FNEG/FABS/FSQRT are all listed.
3319:
3320:		    *** AND THE FIRST CORRECTION OF THIS COMMENT WAS ITSELF AN
3321:		    OVERCLAIM, caught by a review seat within the hour. ***  It
3322:		    said the DECISION still stands because it rests on FSRRA
3323:		    being an approximation rather than on any page number.  But
3324:		    that premise is unsupported by the SAME documents, for the
3325:		    SAME reason: they do not mention FSRRA at all.  Withdrawing
3326:		    a citation and keeping the belief it was offered to support
3327:		    is not a correction, it is the same claim with the evidence
3328:		    removed -- and this project has already recorded that a
3329:		    records-correction round tends to repeat the error it is
3330:		    correcting.
3331:
3332:		    THE HONEST STATE, then: the CODE is unchanged and has been
3333:		    unchanged since #339; what is UNSOURCED is the reason given
3334:		    for it.  Nothing in this tree documents FSRRA's accuracy
3335:		    either way.  Settling it needs an SH-4A manual, which is
3336:		    the document that actually defines the instruction.  Until
3337:		    one is here this comment claims no architectural fact, and
3338:		    the behaviour is recorded as a choice awaiting a source
3339:		    rather than as a conclusion drawn from one.  See the filed
3340:		    row `sh4a4gate` for the separate question of decoding it at
3341:		    all on a modelled SH7750. Wiring
3342:		    it to sh_fp_rm() would round a number that was never the
3343:		    architectural answer to begin with, which buys nothing and
3344:		    implies a precision the instruction does not have. The
3345:		    FPSCR.DN policy still applies and is enforced by #334's
3346:		    macro, which wraps this call like every other.  */
3347:		ieee = ieee_store_float_value(1.0f / sqrt(op1.f), IEEE_FMT_S);
